WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.813
Privacy and training belong
to the agency, end to end.

2
00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:07.000
The privacy baseline applies
at every impact level,

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.856
so a Low system holding the same
personal information carries

4
00:00:10.856 --> 00:00:14.712
the same privacy controls, and
FedRAMP doesn't cover any of them.

5
00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:17.419
The questions are about
authority and purpose:

6
00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:21.304
why the agency collects the information,
whether it told the person,

7
00:00:21.304 --> 00:00:24.426
and whether it published the
system of records notice.

8
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:29.150
The senior privacy official approves
the privacy plan before authorization.

9
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.975
Training is the one family
no configuration can close.

10
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:37.575
Training comes before access, and
awareness is refreshed at least yearly.

11
00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:40.491
Here's the trap: a dashboard
showing ninety-eight

12
00:00:40.491 --> 00:00:43.625
percent completion is a
number with no denominator.

13
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:47.638
The proof is counts per population,
measured against a stated roster,

14
00:00:47.638 --> 00:00:50.525
that someone who didn't
produce them can re-derive.

15
00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:52.220
So who owns all of this?
